        },
        {
          "id": "pub-el-gaz-0046",
          "left": "284px",
          "top": "532px",
          "width": "224px",
          "height": "510px",
          "transform": "none",
          "zIndex": "10",
          "overflow": "visible",
          "type": "text",
          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Merriweather', Georgia, serif; font-size:9.6px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.46; text-align:justify; outline:none;\"><div style=\"font-family:'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:700; color:#111827; margin:0 0 6px 0;\">Rescue Legacy .PUB &amp; .PDF Files</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 11px 0;\">Long-running community presses rarely start from scratch. OpenPublisher includes native import bridges for Microsoft Publisher <b>.pub</b> publications, Word <b>.docx</b> manuscripts, and <b>.pdf</b> proofs directly into editable frames.</div><div style=\"font-family:'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size:12.5px; font-weight:700; color:#111827; margin:4px 0 6px 0;\">Cross-Platform Everywhere</div><div style=\"margin:0;\">Newsrooms run identical documents across <b>Windows</b>, <b>macOS</b>, <b>Linux</b> (Flatpak, AppImage, DEB, and RPM), <b>FreeBSD</b>, static <b>Web</b> browsers, and even legacy <b>Windows XP 32-bit</b> workstations still humming quietly in parish basements.</div></div>",
