          "width": "298px",
          "height": "204px",
          "transform": "none",
          "zIndex": "10",
          "overflow": "visible",
          "type": "text",
          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Merriweather', Georgia, serif; font-size:9.6px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.46; text-align:justify; outline:none;\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 11px 0;\"><span style=\"float:left; font-family:'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size:36px; line-height:0.84; font-weight:700; color:#0f5c57; padding:3px 7px 0 0;\">C</span>ommunity memory travels on printed paper and carefully saved layout files. A school concert program, a small-town heritage walk map, and a parish newsletter are civic artifacts, not rented SaaS inventory.</div><div style=\"margin:0;\">When software vendors convert essential creative tools into metered rentals, a lapsed credit card can sever an entire club from ten years of its own published history.</div></div>",
