          "zIndex": "10",
          "overflow": "visible",
          "type": "text",
          "innerHTML": "<div contenteditable=\"true\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:100%; height:100%; padding:0px; box-sizing:border-box; font-family:'Merriweather', Georgia, serif; font-size:9.6px; color:#1f2937; line-height:1.46; text-align:justify; outline:none;\"><div style=\"margin:0 0 11px 0;\"><span style=\"float:left; font-family:'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif; font-size:36px; line-height:0.84; font-weight:700; color:#0f5c57; padding:3px 7px 0 0;\">T</span>ype has always carried a newspaper's personality before the first sentence is read. OpenPublisher pairs curated <b>Font Schemes</b> such as Newsletter Editorial, Classic Serif, and Modern Business with custom pairing previews.</div><div style=\"margin:0 0 11px 0;\">Inside the Insert tab, editors browse over <b>3,000 vector clipart</b> illustrations, decorative antique <b>Page Borders</b>, and <b>Retro &amp; 3D WordArt</b> that automatically bake cleanly for physical presses.</div><div style=\"margin:0;\">Best of all, swapping a publication's complete heading-and-body personality takes one click from Page Design without losing text alignments.</div></div>",
